Two :CLASS definitions in one file (diag.one_class_per_file, error, on
the second :CLASS only). The first :CLASS is the file's first statement,
so class_or_script stays silent.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Alpha;
:DECLARE nCount;

:PROCEDURE Work;
	Me:nCount += 1;
:ENDPROC;

:CLASS Beta;
:DECLARE sName;

:PROCEDURE Name;
	:RETURN Me:sName;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Alpha;
:DECLARE nCount;

:PROCEDURE Work;
	Me:nCount += 1;
:ENDPROC;

:CLASS Beta;
:DECLARE sName;

:PROCEDURE Name;
	:RETURN Me:sName;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
8:1-8:7 error one_class_per_file: Only one ':CLASS' definition is allowed per file
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
8:1-8:7 error one_class_per_file: Only one ':CLASS' definition is allowed per file
9:1-9:9 info class_member_order: Class members must be ordered as ':DECLARE' fields, then methods
